WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.050
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:04.270
- [Narrator] In the midst
of the George Floyd tragedy,

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.730
hundreds of surfers in New York's Rockaway

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:10.010
came together in their
own way to honor his life

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:13.032
and to protest against racial injustices.

00:00:13.032 --> 00:00:16.181
- [Group] Black lives matter!

00:00:16.181 --> 00:00:17.440
- When things happen in the community,

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:18.973
you gotta speak up on it.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.360
When you're silent, you're violent.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.060
That's why I speak my mind,
so you don't always have

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:25.570
to listen, but for you
young people, listen.

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:27.320
And they came and it was beautiful.

00:00:31.449 --> 00:00:33.380
(uplifting music)

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:35.440
I'm Lou Harris. I'm the East Coast founder

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:36.870
of the Black Surfing Association

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.410
and we provide free surf
lessons, free skateboard lessons

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:40.663
for the kids of Rockaway.

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:43.840
A lot of kids don't have
money to save for a board.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.610
That's why I'm glad I get donations

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:48.140
and I get to give them away for free.

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:52.355
We'll do surfing on
Saturdays from 8 to 10,

00:00:52.355 --> 00:00:54.520
and then we'll do skateboarding
from 11 to one Saturday

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:55.353
and same things on Sundays

00:00:55.353 --> 00:00:56.923
and during the summer, it's everyday.

00:00:58.921 --> 00:01:01.690
(cheerful music)

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:03.808
I got into surfing cause
I moved here 15 years ago

00:01:03.808 --> 00:01:06.258
and I needed an outlet,
I needed something to do.

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:10.250
I walked up to the boardwalk
on beach 90th street

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:11.303
and I saw people surfing.

00:01:11.303 --> 00:01:12.870
I was like whoa.

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:13.703
They surf here?

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:17.623
I taught myself how to surf

00:01:17.623 --> 00:01:19.680
and I've been surfing ever since.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.910
You know, I surf big waves,
small waves, hurricane waves.

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:24.500
I remember there wasn't
too many black surfers.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.400
It was me and maybe a
couple of other kids.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.280
These young, you know, African
Americans they live here

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:30.913
and they should know what
goes on in their own backyard.

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:34.980
You should know the sandbar,
you should know the drop offs,

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:36.520
you should know all that.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:38.140
It's good for young kids to get exposed

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:40.190
because I want kids to see
that the line up doesn't have

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:41.270
to be particularly white all the time.

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:42.910
That's what it usually is.

00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:45.140
It's great to see a Black
face here and there,

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:46.913
Spanish face here, Asian face here.

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:52.700
- [Narrator] Lou's mission
uses surfing not only

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:56.090
to empower kids in his
community, but also as a tool

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:57.586
to bring people together.

00:01:57.586 --> 00:01:58.419
(inspirational music)

00:01:58.419 --> 00:02:01.010
And recently, he did exactly that.

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:03.420
Lou organized a paddle
out to raise awareness

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:05.440
for Black Lives Matter.

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:08.750
- A paddle out is most of
the time when a surfer dies.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:11.630
You paddle out into a
circle and you throw flowers

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:13.630
into the water and you splash the water.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:16.370
Today was a great paddle out

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:19.033
because we got to say all
the black lives matter.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:23.050
I thought it was gonna
be a hundred people.

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:25.913
This was over 300 and I'm still in shock.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:32.850
I'm just happy who came and,
like again, I'm blown away,

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:34.400
but you know white people,

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:35.570
they're the one starting the chant.

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:37.843
They're the one saying
no justice, no peace.

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:40.350
It's Black people getting killed,

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:43.080
but this was predominately white people

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:43.913
and they're beautiful people

00:02:43.913 --> 00:02:45.866
and they're getting sick of it too.

00:02:45.866 --> 00:02:47.699
- [Group] Don't shoot!

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:51.330
- When people see me, you
know, they don't see a surfer.

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:52.380
They see a Black guy.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:56.283
But this is my backyard and I love it.

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:59.950
Today was probably the most successful day

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:01.330
of my life being an African American man.

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:06.023
I mean, my little voice started
a 300 person movement today.

